.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pepe-slack 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-slack \- Connect pepe to Slack from here, so \-\-slack keeps a message there up to date as a run goes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe slack\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect pepe to Slack from here, so \-\-slack keeps a message there up to date as a run goes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pepe\-slack\-connect(1)
Make pepe\*(Aqs Slack app, take its token, pick a channel, post a test (the default)
.TP
pepe\-slack\-status(1)
What is connected, checked with Slack
.TP
pepe\-slack\-test(1)
Post a test message
.TP
pepe\-slack\-serve(1)
Answer the buttons and /pepe: run this directory\*(Aqs saved tests for the people allowed, and stop them
.TP
pepe\-slack\-allow(1)
Who may press the buttons and use /pepe: @names, Slack ids, or * for anyone in the channel
.TP
pepe\-slack\-forget(1)
Remove the kept token
.TP
pepe\-slack\-manifest(1)
Print the app\*(Aqs manifest, for Slack\*(Aqs "From a manifest"
.TP
pepe\-slack\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
